    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 15 Church Gate is an exceptional four bedroom detached family residence, occupying a prime position at the end of a quiet cul-de-sac in this highly convenient location. Benefiting from a large corner site the property's outstanding south-facing rear garden is undoubtedly a defining feature, offering an abundance of space for family life, outdoor entertaining and recreation, while enjoying sunshine throughout the day.\n \nBeautifully presented and generously proportioned throughout, the accommodation has been thoughtfully designed to accommodate the evolving needs of modern family living. At its heart lies a superb L-shaped open-plan kitchen, dining and family room, complemented by two additional reception rooms, creating a home that effortlessly balances everyday practicality with comfortable entertaining.\n \nA welcoming entrance hall immediately sets the tone, featuring porcelain tiled flooring, elegant ceiling coving and useful understairs storage. Off the hall is a conveniently positioned guest WC. To the front, the living room is a warm and inviting space with solid timber flooring and a charming wood-burning stove set on a slate hearth, creating a wonderful focal point. Glazed double doors provide a seamless connection to the kitchen and family area beyond. Opposite, a versatile playroom/study offers excellent flexibility and could equally serve as a home office, children's playroom, TV room or additional reception space.\n \nThe impressive open-plan kitchen, dining and family room spans the entire rear of the house and is perfectly designed for both day-to-day family life and larger gatherings. The kitchen is fitted with an extensive range of shaker-style cabinetry, quality stone worktops and a large cooking range. Generous dining and family areas overlook the garden, while large windows and glazed doors flood the room with natural light and create a seamless connection between the indoor and outdoor spaces.\n \nUpstairs, the principal bedroom is a spacious double room positioned to the front of the property and benefits from an extensive range of built-in wardrobes together with a private en-suite shower room. Three further bedrooms provide excellent family accommodation, comprising two additional double bedrooms and a generous single bedroom all of which boast built in storage. A fully tiled family bathroom, complete with Jacuzzi bath and electric shower, completes the first-floor accommodation.\n \nOutside, the magnificent rear garden sets this home apart. Exceptionally private and enjoying a sunny south-facing orientation, it is laid predominantly in lawn and provides ample space for children to play while still leaving plenty of room for gardening and entertaining. Thoughtfully designed seating areas allow the owners to enjoy the sun at different times of the day, with a raised deck capturing the evening westerly sunshine and a separate patio area benefiting from the morning easterly aspect.\n \nThe practicality of the property is further enhanced by vehicular side access leading to a cobblelock driveway, providing excellent convenience and additional parking options. A substantial detached wooden cabin offers valuable storage and utility space, complemented by a separate garden shed for further outdoor storage requirements. Of particular note is the fully wired workshop, an exceptionally versatile addition that could serve a variety of purposes including a home office, gym, studio, games room or creative workspace. Together, these ancillary buildings significantly enhance the functionality of the property and cater effortlessly to the demands of modern family living. Given the exceptional size of the side and rear gardens, the property may also offer potential for a separate dwelling, subject to the necessary planning permissions, making this an exciting opportunity for those seeking future development potential.\nCombining spacious accommodation, exceptional gardens and a superb position within this sought-after development, No. 15 Church Gate represents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a truly impressive family home. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nComposite hall door, porcelain tiles, ceiling coving, radiator cover, under-stairs storage.\n\nGuest WC - 1.02m x 2.09m\nPorcelain tiles, wc, wash hand basin with store, spot lighting.\n\nLiving Room - 3.41m x 5.03m\nSolid wooden flooring, wood burning stove, slate hearth and stone mantle piece, ceiling coving, glass paneled double doors to;\n\nKitchen/Dining/Family Room - 7.86m x 5.97m\nWalnut flooring, ceiling coving, radiator cover, eye and floor level units, 6 ring electric hob, range, extractor fan, provision for large fridge, under cabinet lighting, stone counter tops and window sills, double doors to garden and side access.\n\nPlay Room/Study - 2.71m x 4.56m\nLarge window looking to the front, wooden flooring.\n\nLanding - 3.83m x 2.60m\nStira to attic, access to all principle rooms.\n\nMain Bedroom - 4.84m x 2.78m\nLarge double bedroom, looking to the front, extensive range of built-in wardrobes, access to;\n\nEn-Suite - 2.12m x 2.12m\nFully tiled, corner step-in shower, wash hand basin, unit with fitted mirror and storage, WC, window.\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.78m x 4.84m\nDouble bedroom, looking to the front, access to wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.23m x 2.93m\nDouble bedroom, looking to the rear, built-in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.14m x 3.43m\nLarge single bedroom, looking to the rear, built-in wardrobe.\n\nBathroom - 2.56m x 1.78m\nJacuzzi bath, Triton electric shower, fully tiled, WC, chrome heated towel, sink with storage.\n\nGarden - \nExceptionally large rear garden laid mainly in lawn with vehicular side access leading to a cobblelock driveway. Large detached cabin currently in use as a storage and utility room, with an additional large detached wooden shed providing further outdoor storage. Raised deck area captures the westerly sunshine, while a separate seating area enjoys a morning easterly aspect. Wired outdoor workshop and wired outdoor lighting. Potential for further development, including the construction of a separate dwelling, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\n"
